  [PASS] B1a (validation) the deprojection is self-consistent: numerically projecting the Prugniel-Simien density back along the line of sight returns the exact Sersic n = 4 projected-mass law   (projected/exact at R/R_e = 0.3, 0.6, 1, 2: 1.0050, 1.0013, 0.9998, 0.9988)
  [PASS] B1b (validation) the projected phantom mass at the Einstein radius does not depend on where the line of sight is truncated: the deep-MOND phantom's rho ~ 1/r^2 makes the cylinder integrand fall as 1/r^2, so a 200 kpc and a 20 Mpc cylinder give the same answer   (boost with the line of sight cut at 200 kpc / 1 Mpc / 3 Mpc / 20 Mpc = 1.1504 / 1.1545 / 1.1551 / 1.1554)
